    "ECGrav", "status" -> "None", "summary" -> 
    "Branchedness[g_Graph, n_Integer] Given a graph g and a dimension n, it \
computes the rms value of the degree of the n-facets, minus 3/2. This \
quantity will be zero for pseudo manifolds if n is the purity of the graph \
minus one since all codimension 1 faces have degree 1 or 2. \
Branchedness[g_Graph] Given a graph g with dimension n, it computes the rms \
value of the degree of the n-facets, minus 3/2. This quantity will be zero \
for pseudo manifolds if n is the purity of the graph minus one since all \
codimension 1 faces have degree 1 or 2. Branchedness[Amat_List, n_Integer] \
Given a graph as an adjacency matrix Amat and a dimension n, it computes the \
rms value of the degree of the n-facets, minus 3/2. This quantity will be \
zero for pseudo manifolds if n is the purity of the graph minus one since all \
codimension 1 faces have degree 1 or 2. Branchedness[Amat] Given a graph as \
an adjacency matrix Amat with dimension n, it computes the rms value of the \
degree of the n-facets, minus 3/2. This quantity will be zero for pseudo \
manifolds if n is the purity of the graph minus one since all codimension 1 \
faces have degree 1 or 2. ", "synonyms" -> {}, "tabletags" -> {}, "title" -> 
